{"mcp-recv":{"id":1,"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":{"tools":[{"description":"Delegate a self-contained task to a child agent, in a new thread under this one. The child starts at once and the call returns; each time its turn ends done or failed, its report comes to this thread as a new message, so do not wait or poll for it. Folder, permissions and model inherit unless you pick a model. This thread's history is not copied, so the task must stand on its own. The user sees the child and can open it. A child cannot gain broader permissions. Reuse client_request_id to retry the same task safely; each new task needs a new one.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"client_request_id":{"maxLength":256,"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"effort":{"description":"The child's reasoning effort; else this thread's.","type":"string"},"model":{"description":"The child's model, by the id this thread's agent knows it by; else this thread's.","type":"string"},"task":{"description":"The child's first message: a complete brief.","maxLength":120000,"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"title":{"description":"A short name for the child's thread.","maxLength":512,"type":"string"}},"required":["task"],"type":"object"},"name":"delegate_task"},{"_meta":{"anthropic/alwaysLoad":true},"description":"Ask the user for secrets (API keys, tokens, passwords) in a private card, instead of asking in chat. Batch every value you know you need into one call. The call waits until the user answers. You never see the values: each is saved in a private file, and an env script exports them all. Never put a value in a command line, a file you write, a log or a reply, and never print the files or the environment.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"client_request_id":{"description":"Reuse it to retry the same request; a new request needs a new one.","maxLength":256,"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"env_file":{"description":"Also write the values to this dotenv file in the thread's folder, such as .env.local, for an app that reads it. Git must ignore it.","type":"string"},"fields":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"label":{"description":"What the card calls it, such as \"OpenAI API key\".","maxLength":120,"type":"string"},"name":{"description":"The environment variable the value is given as, such as OPENAI_API_KEY.","pattern":"^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*$","type":"string"},"url":{"description":"An https page where the user gets the value.","type":"string"}},"required":["name"],"type":"object"},"maxItems":8,"minItems":1,"type":"array"},"reason":{"description":"What the values are for and where the user gets them, in a sentence or two.","maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["reason","fields"],"type":"object"},"name":"request_credentials"}]}}}
